# vdev.manifest — TSR-VDEV-001 expected virtual-device set for the QHV guest.
#
# Phase 1 (study-level). One vdev id per line; '#' comments and blank lines
# ignored. These are the vdevs the no-network g2.conf in post_start.custom
# declares for the guest synthetic platform (ARMv8_Foundation_Model). The
# verifier reconciles this DECLARED set against what the boot log shows the
# guest actually instantiated.
#
# Field 1: vdev id (matched in g2.conf / boot log)
# Field 2: guest-side presence token expected in the boot log when the vdev
#          is live (or "-" if presence cannot be confirmed from the serial
#          log on this leg — recorded as presence-unknown, not failure).
#
# NOTE: the net path is INERT on this leg by design. virtio-net is
# intentionally ABSENT from g2.conf, so it is NOT manifested here — see
# TCR-HYP-001 least-vdev. If a future build adds it, add it here too.

# pl011 / virtio-console: no per-device token is matched for them in the
# serial log, so presence is recorded as UNKNOWN ('-') rather than asserted or
# false-failed. virtio-blk presence is matched on the guest's devb
# "Direct-Access ... VIRTIO" line, so it carries a real token.
pl011           -
virtio-console  -
virtio-blk      VIRTIO
